.git
.cursor
.github
.env
.env.*
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/cdk.out
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# The web app is not part of the API image, but pnpm validates the lockfile
# against every project in the workspace, so its manifest has to stay in the
# build context or `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` fails on a missing project.
apps/web/**
!apps/web/package.json

assets
docs
sim
test-results
*.md
*.tgz

# Local caches and QA output. None of it is source, all of it is gitignored, and
# together it was 1.6 GB of build context: CDK stages the whole context into
# infra/cdk.out and uploads it as an image asset, so every deploy was carrying a
# Playwright browser bundle and a folder of screenshots to ECR. It is also how
# .shots/ probe scripts ended up inside cdk.out, where `pnpm lint`'s
# dangling-import scan finds them and fails on relative paths that cannot resolve
# from a staged copy.
.pnpm-store
.pw-browsers
.shots
.nm-trash-*
*.log
